{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.12","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":129716}],"dockerImageVersionId":31328,"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/sarcasmos/nvidia-nemotron-model-reasoning-challenge?scriptVersionId=307496783\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<div style=\"\n  background: #0d0d0d;\n  border: 0.5px solid #1e1e1e;\n  border-radius: 14px;\n  padding: 40px 40px 36px 40px;\n  font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;\n  margin: 10px 0 24px 0;\n\">\n\n  <!-- Section label -->\n  <div style=\"\n    display: inline-block;\n    background: #1a1a2e;\n    border: 0.5px solid #534AB7;\n    color: #9F97EC;\n    font-size: 10px;\n    letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    padding: 4px 14px;\n    border-radius: 20px;\n    margin-bottom: 22px;\n  \">📖 Notebook Introduction</div>\n\n  <!-- Main heading -->\n  <h2 style=\"\n    color: #e0e0e0;\n    font-size: 20px;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 20px 0;\n    letter-spacing: 0.03em;\n    line-height: 1.4;\n    border-left: 3px solid #534AB7;\n    padding-left: 14px;\n  \">NVIDIA Nemotron Model Reasoning Challenge<br>\n    <span style=\"font-size: 14px; color: #555; font-weight: 400;\">\n      Exploratory Data Analysis — What This Notebook Does\n    </span>\n  </h2>\n\n  <!-- Paragraph 1 -->\n  <div style=\"\n    background: #0f0f0f;\n    border: 0.5px solid #1e1e1e;\n    border-left: 2px solid #534AB7;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    padding: 18px 22px;\n    margin-bottom: 16px;\n  \">\n    <div style=\"\n      color: #555;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      margin-bottom: 10px;\n    \">▸ About the Competition</div>\n    <p style=\"\n      color: #888;\n      font-size: 13px;\n      line-height: 1.9;\n      margin: 0;\n    \">\n      This notebook presents a structured and in-depth exploratory data analysis of the\n      <span style=\"color: #9F97EC; font-weight: 600;\">NVIDIA Nemotron Model Reasoning Challenge</span>\n      dataset hosted on Kaggle. The competition centers around a uniquely challenging problem — training a model\n      to identify and apply hidden transformation rules across a variety of logical reasoning puzzle domains.\n      Unlike conventional NLP or classification tasks, this challenge demands that the model reason from a small\n      set of input-output examples embedded directly inside each prompt, infer the underlying rule, and then\n      apply it correctly to a new unseen input. The puzzles span multiple domains including\n      <span style=\"color: #9F97EC;\">8-bit binary manipulation</span>,\n      <span style=\"color: #5DCAA5;\">text encryption and Caesar-style ciphers</span>,\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27;\">algebraic equation solving</span>, and\n      <span style=\"color: #D85A30;\">sequence pattern recognition</span>,\n      all wrapped inside a consistent narrative framing set in Alice's Wonderland.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Paragraph 2 -->\n  <div style=\"\n    background: #0f0f0f;\n    border: 0.5px solid #1e1e1e;\n    border-left: 2px solid #0F6E56;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    padding: 18px 22px;\n    margin-bottom: 16px;\n  \">\n    <div style=\"\n      color: #555;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      margin-bottom: 10px;\n    \">▸ About the Dataset</div>\n    <p style=\"\n      color: #888;\n      font-size: 13px;\n      line-height: 1.9;\n      margin: 0;\n    \">\n      The dataset consists of two files —\n      <span style=\"color: #5DCAA5; font-family: monospace;\">train.csv</span> and\n      <span style=\"color: #5DCAA5; font-family: monospace;\">test.csv</span>.\n      The training file contains a unique identifier, the full puzzle prompt including examples and the target\n      query, and the ground truth answer. The test file contains only the identifier and the prompt, with answers\n      withheld for evaluation. The total dataset weighs approximately\n      <span style=\"color: #ccc;\">3.07 MB</span>\n      and is licensed under\n      <span style=\"color: #ccc;\">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</span>,\n      making it freely usable with proper attribution. What makes this competition particularly interesting from\n      a modeling perspective is that the submission is not a predictions CSV but rather a\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27; font-weight: 600;\">LoRA adapter file</span>\n      packaged as\n      <span style=\"color: #5DCAA5; font-family: monospace;\">submission.zip</span>,\n      meaning the competition is directly evaluating the quality of a fine-tuned model rather than its outputs\n      on a fixed test set.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Paragraph 3 -->\n  <div style=\"\n    background: #0f0f0f;\n    border: 0.5px solid #1e1e1e;\n    border-left: 2px solid #854F0B;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    padding: 18px 22px;\n    margin-bottom: 16px;\n  \">\n    <div style=\"\n      color: #555;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      margin-bottom: 10px;\n    \">▸ Purpose of This Notebook</div>\n    <p style=\"\n      color: #888;\n      font-size: 13px;\n      line-height: 1.9;\n      margin: 0;\n    \">\n      Before any model training or fine-tuning can begin, it is essential to deeply understand what the data\n      looks like, how the puzzles are structured, what patterns exist in the prompts and answers, and whether\n      there are any biases or imbalances across puzzle types that could affect training. That is exactly the\n      purpose of this notebook. We will walk through the dataset systematically — loading and inspecting the\n      raw files, engineering features like\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27;\">puzzle type classification</span>,\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27;\">answer type classification</span>,\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27;\">prompt length</span>,\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27;\">word count</span>, and\n      <span style=\"color: #EF9F27;\">example count</span>,\n      then visualizing all of these dimensions through a series of purpose-built charts including distribution\n      histograms, donut charts, horizontal bar charts, box plots, a radar complexity chart, a keyword frequency\n      analysis, and a full correlation heatmap. Every visualization is rendered on a\n      <span style=\"color: #ccc;\">dark background</span>\n      for clarity and professionalism. By the end of this analysis, we will have a thorough understanding of\n      the data that directly informs how to structure a LoRA fine-tuning run for maximum effectiveness on this\n      reasoning task.\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- What to expect row -->\n  <div style=\"\n    background: #0f0f0f;\n    border: 0.5px solid #1e1e1e;\n    border-radius: 8px;\n    padding: 18px 22px;\n  \">\n    <div style=\"\n      color: #555;\n      font-size: 10px;\n      letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      margin-bottom: 14px;\n    \">▸ What to Expect in This Notebook</div>\n    <div style=\"\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;\n      gap: 10px;\n    \">\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;\">\n        <span style=\"color:#534AB7;font-size:14px;margin-top:1px;\">◆</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#666;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;\">Raw data loading and structural inspection</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;\">\n        <span style=\"color:#0F6E56;font-size:14px;margin-top:1px;\">◆</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#666;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;\">Puzzle and answer type classification</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;\">\n        <span style=\"color:#854F0B;font-size:14px;margin-top:1px;\">◆</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#666;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;\">Prompt and answer length distributions</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;\">\n        <span style=\"color:#993C1D;font-size:14px;margin-top:1px;\">◆</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#666;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;\">Box plots and radar complexity scoring</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;\">\n        <span style=\"color:#534AB7;font-size:14px;margin-top:1px;\">◆</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#666;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;\">Top keyword frequency across all prompts</span>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;\">\n        <span style=\"color:#0F6E56;font-size:14px;margin-top:1px;\">◆</span>\n        <span style=\"color:#666;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;\">Correlation heatmap and full dashboard</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.patches as mpatches\nimport matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec\nfrom matplotlib.colors import LinearSegmentedColormap\nimport seaborn as sns\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport re\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\nplt.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = '#0d0d0d'\nplt.rcParams['axes.facecolor'] = '#111111'\nplt.rcParams['axes.edgecolor'] = '#2a2